This paper investigates the normalized ground state solution for the given biharmonic Choquard type equation \begin{align*}
  \begin{split}
  \left\{
  \begin{array}{ll}
  \Delta^2u-\beta\Delta u=\lambda u+\left(\frac{1}{|x|^\mu}*F(u)\right)f(u),
  \quad\mbox{in}\ \ \mathbb{R}^4,
  \displaystyle\int_{\mathbb{R}^4}|u|^2dx=c^2,\quad u\in H^2(\mathbb{R}^4),
  \end{array}
  \right.
  \end{split}
  \end{align*} under specific constraints and growth conditions for $\beta$, $\lambda$, and $f$, and we leverage a homotopy-based minimax principle to establish the existence of a normalized ground state solution for this equation. Furthermore, we demonstrate that the obtained solution exhibits the maximum critical value among all critical points within a certain functional space. Additionally, we analyze the asymptotic behavior of the solution as $x\rightarrow\infty$. Finally, we discuss how the obtained results can be applied to derive the existence of multiple solutions for the related nonlinear biharmonic equations and systems. This study is an extension of the research by the authors on the biharmonic Choquard type equations and systems in \cite{BZ20}, \cite{BZ21}, \cite{BZ22}, \cite{BZ23}, and provides new insights into the related mathematical problems. This work was partially supported by the National Natural Science Foundation of China (grant no. 11971071) and the Natural Science Foundation of Jiangxi Province (grant no. 2018AA017140).} \end{scriptsize}  Laster L. M., Zeng W.  Journal of Differential Equations  https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jmaa.2021.07.050 First published online 16 Jul 2021. 2021. 7. 50. 6. 26. 2021. 7. 16. 10.1016/j.jmaa.2021.07.050. 104672. 2021.  https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0022039621005174. 2. 3.
